title: $:/plugins/mblackman/mermaid/readme

! Mermaid for TiddlyWiki5

Modern, self-contained, 100% offline ''Mermaid.js (v11+)'' diagram rendering for TiddlyWiki5.

!! Features

* ''100% Offline:'' Bundles Mermaid v11+ with all diagram types inlined. No external CDNs or network requests.
* ''Active Palette Integration:'' Diagrams automatically adopt your active TiddlyWiki palette colors (`primary`, `background`, `foreground`, `border`), dynamically updating whenever you switch palettes.
* ''Legibility-First Architecture:'' Guarantees high text contrast across all node types, categorical scales (`cScale0..11`), git branch labels, and notes, avoiding the unreadable color combinations in stock Mermaid.
* ''Curated Theme Library:'' Choose between Palette Sync (`auto`), High Contrast (WCAG AAA >= 7:1), Technical Blueprint, Monochrome, Modern Mermaid v11 themes (`redux`, `neo`), or classic stock themes.
* ''Unified WikiText & Markdown:'' Render diagrams inside standard fenced code blocks (<code>```mermaid</code>) in both native WikiText and Markdown tiddlers ([[$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/markdown]]).
* ''Direct Widget Support:'' Embed diagrams anywhere using `<$mermaid text="..." />` or inline `<$mermaid>...</$mermaid>`.
* ''Mermaid v11 Diagrams:'' Supports Flowcharts, Sequence Diagrams, Class Diagrams, State Diagrams, ER Diagrams, Mindmaps, Timelines, GitGraphs, Pie Charts, Quadrants, XY Charts, Kanban, Architecture Diagrams, C4, Sankey, Packet, Block, and more.
* ''Suite Design System Ready:'' Fully compatible with the TiddlyWiki Productivity Suite (`MASTER.md`) and Slipstream theme.

!! Usage

!!! 1. Fenced Code Blocks (WikiText & Markdown)

````markdown
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Start] --> B{Decision}
    B -->|Yes| C[Proceed]
    B -->|No| D[Halt]
```
````

!!! 2. `<$mermaid>` Widget

```html
<$mermaid text="graph TD; A-->B;"/>
```

Or with inline body:

```html
<$mermaid>
mindmap
  root((Central Idea))
    Topic 1
      Subtopic A
      Subtopic B
    Topic 2
</$mermaid>
```

!! Attributes

|!Attribute |!Description |!Default |
|`text` or `source` |The Mermaid diagram definition string |`""` |
|`theme` |Theme name (see below) |`auto` |
|`align` |Container alignment: `left`, `center`, or `right` |`center` |
|`class` |Optional additional CSS class names for styling |`""` |
|`security-level` |Mermaid security level: `loose`, `strict`, `antiscript`, or `sandbox` |`loose` |

!! Available Themes

* ''Dynamic & Legibility-First:''
** `auto` (Default): Dynamically maps colors from your active TiddlyWiki palette with contrast safeguards.
** `palette`: Explicitly bind to the active TiddlyWiki palette.
** `high-contrast`: WCAG AAA compliance (>= 7:1 contrast ratio) with bold borders and ultra-crisp text.
** `technical` / `blueprint`: Clean technical blueprint theme with high-visibility cyan/slate styling.
** `monochrome`: Publication-grade grayscale with distinct solid fills and clear text.
* ''Modern Mermaid v11:''
** `redux-auto`, `redux`, `redux-dark`: Mermaid v11 modern minimalist theme.
** `redux-color-auto`, `redux-color`, `redux-color-dark`: Modern colorful palette with crisp typography.
** `neo-auto`, `neo`, `neo-dark`: Soft pastel tones with dark mode support.
* ''Classic Mermaid:''
** `default`: Classic Mermaid light theme.
** `dark`: Classic Mermaid dark theme.
** `forest`: Classic green tones.
** `neutral`: Classic grayscale.
** `base`: Unstyled base theme.
